# Build context for mx-test-framework's image is this directory rather than the
# project's own, because the image needs mx-common and mx-launcher/ui-design
# next to it (both are `file:` dependencies).
#
# The cost of that choice is that Docker tars up every sibling project on its
# way to the daemon. mx-launcher alone carries four node_modules trees, one of
# them an Electron desktop app's — so without this file, `manage.sh deploy`
# ships gigabytes before it runs a single build step.
#
# mx-insight-hub builds from its own directory with `--build-context`, so these
# rules do not affect it.
#
# Listed as explicit exclusions rather than an allowlist with `!` negations:
# negation ordering in .dockerignore is easy to get subtly wrong, and the
# failure mode is a missing file inside the image rather than an error here.

**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.runtime
**/coverage
**/*.log

# Never ship credentials into a build context.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Regenerated inside the image by ui-design/scripts/build.mjs, which uses only
# node built-ins. Excluding it keeps a stale local build out of the image.
**/dist

# Siblings the Dockerfile never copies. mx-launcher/ui-design is the one part of
# mx-launcher the image needs, so the rest of it is excluded piece by piece.
mx-insight-hub/
mx-launcher/demos/
mx-launcher/deploy/
mx-launcher/desktop/
mx-launcher/docs/
mx-launcher/packages/
mx-launcher/scripts/
mx-launcher/server/
mx-launcher/setup/
mx-launcher/site-slots/

# Local scratch and editor state.
**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/tmp/
